/-
WeilCert: a machine-checked window of Weil positivity.

Main result `weil_window_positive`: every rational 12x12 matrix M whose entries
lie entrywise within 1/10^20 of the explicit rational matrix mRat (given by the
integer data aFun below divided by 10^24) has a strictly positive quadratic
form: 0 < x . (M x) for all x != 0.

Interpretation (Bridge Proposition, proved by exact-rational reduction of the
archimedean kernel plus 220-bit outward-rounded interval arithmetic — see
THEOREMS.md): the truncated Weil quadratic form of zeta at support L = 497/200
in the unnormalized Legendre basis P_0..P_11 of test functions supported in
[-497/800, 497/800] is such a matrix.  Hence Weil positivity holds on that
explicit 12-dimensional space of test functions — a support window in which
BOTH primes 2 and 3 contribute.  The certificate is an integer congruence
  cInt^2 * B = W^T * diag(g) * W,   Winv * W = fInt * 1,   g > 0,
with B = A - 120000 * 1, verified below by kernel computation (`decide`);
no floating point, no trusted external tools, no axioms beyond Lean's kernel.
-/
